  body: "# Industrial Injuries decisions and medical advice\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe source describes
    a 5 July 1999 change to decisions made on behalf of the Secretary of State by lay decision makers, using all
    evidence including advice from doctors.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe date is a source-stated procedural
    transition, not the PDF publication date. Medical expertise informs the decision; it does not confer adjudication
    authority on a model. Complete current procedures and delegated responsibilities need verification.\n\n## Inspected
    passages\n\n- [DMG 64060, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/664b1c4dbd01f5ed32793e51/dmg-chapter-64-background-to-the-industrial-scheme.pdf#page=6).\n\
    - [DMG 64061, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/664b1c4dbd01f5ed32793e51/dmg-chapter-64-background-to-the-industrial-scheme.pdf#page=6).\n\
    - [DMG 64062, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/664b1c4dbd01f5ed32793e51/dmg-chapter-64-background-to-the-industrial-scheme.pdf#page=6).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol11-ch64`:
    PDF `6397b92476509f66c98cbd574ef4692bf1888e41fe7da4a9ec227b7a13a62b78`; extracted pages `2bbe57d32fca42027ea6a81e508bda907df0d56da34c4d59ba73862530a659e8`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:33.768652Z`.\n- `dmg-vol11-ch69`: PDF `3bbd376d12fc0a6633010680e88d11efdf7f5b34dde311016a073e80ac3e56b8`;
    extracted pages `fcaf30907d52d71cc7473cf40c8c876469efc3f8d18f7f9af7b3d32bf5016d95`; acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:34.033473Z`.\n"
  resource:
    https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/664b1c4dbd01f5ed32793e51/dmg-chapter-64-background-to-the-industrial-scheme.pdf#page=6
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-decision-maker
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source expressly identifies the DM and the Secretary of State authority behind the
      decision.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch64/0006
      quote: "64061 From 5.7.99 all decisions will be made on behalf of the Secretary of State. This replaces the\n\
        system under which some decisions were made by independent adjudication officers and some on\nbehalf of
        the Secretary of State.\n\n\n\nLay decision making"
      locator: DMG 64061
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch64/0006
      quote: "64062 From 5.7.99 decisions on entitlement to benefits in the II scheme will be made by lay DMs\n\
        employed by DWP. Decisions on entitlement to benefit will be made by DMs on all the evidence,\nincluding
        advice from doctors."
      locator: DMG 64062
  - target: term/iidb-medical-nonmedical-questions
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The detailed IIDB chapter separates medical and non-medical questions within an outcome
      decision.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch69/0006
      quote: "69020 DMs will give an outcome decision on the claim which consists of a statement to the effect that\n\
        the claimant is either entitled or not entitled to benefit. In arriving at an outcome decision, the DM must\n\
        consider various questions. For IIDB, these questions fall into two categories\n\n\n1. non medical questions
        such as employed earners employment, rate of benefit 1and\n\n\n2. medical questions such as diagnosis, relevant
        loss of faculty and disablement assessment.\n\n\nNote: See DMG Chapter 01 for further guidance on IIDB decisions.\n\
        \n\n                                                                                       1 SS CB Act 92,
        s 94"
      locator: DMG 69020
